From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] spirv: OpenGL's SPIR-V fragment shaders take gl_FragCoord from the lower left

NVIDIA's OpenGL gives a SPIR-V fragment shader gl_FragCoord from the lower left whatever origin it declares
(OriginUpperLeft has no effect there; checked on the host's driver: dFdy(gl_FragCoord.y) stays positive, with a GLSL
layout(origin_upper_left) it turns negative); Mesa honoured the declaration. Applications are written against those
drivers: GravityMark's OpenGL renderer declares OriginUpperLeft and fetches its final picture by gl_FragCoord.y, so it
showed upside down. In the OpenGL environment the origin is now lower left; Vulkan's SPIR-V is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c b/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c
index bc5e1f8..e1f7695 100644
--- a/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c
+++ b/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c
@@ -5079,8 +5079,12 @@ vtn_handle_execution_mode(struct vtn_builder *b, struct vtn_value *entry_point,
    case SpvExecutionModeOriginUpperLeft:
    case SpvExecutionModeOriginLowerLeft:
       vtn_assert(b->shader->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT);
+      /* WinBoat: OpenGL's SPIR-V shaders get gl_FragCoord from the lower left whatever they declare, as NVIDIA's GL
+       * gives it (OriginUpperLeft has no effect there; Mesa honoured it): applications are written against those
+       * drivers. GravityMark's OpenGL renderer declares OriginUpperLeft and fetches its final picture by
+       * gl_FragCoord.y: upside down here */
       b->shader->info.fs.origin_upper_left =
-         (mode->exec_mode == SpvExecutionModeOriginUpperLeft);
+         (mode->exec_mode == SpvExecutionModeOriginUpperLeft) && b->options->environment != NIR_SPIRV_OPENGL;
       break;
 
    case SpvExecutionModeEarlyFragmentTests:
